#!/usr/bin/env harding
#
# NotFound.hrd - NotFound class.

NotFound := Error derive
# NotFound reports an access-style lookup that found nothing where the caller
# required something present: a Table or Library keyed read, or a named binding.
# It sits under Error because a missing key in an access lookup is normally a
# programming error, not a value to test.
# Search-style lookups (indexOf:, detect:, findFirst:, findLast:) keep answering
# nil, because there absence is a normal result; use at:ifAbsent: or
# detect:ifNone: when a miss is expected.
